WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.331
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:12.478
Today, Studio's settings, and the Creator API,

5
00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:16.378
which lets you build a world without ever opening Studio.

6
00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.639
The gear at the bottom left opens Settings.

7
00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:25.448
The first switch decides what Studio opens on: the world and mod picker,

8
00:00:25.448 --> 00:00:27.786
or the last world you were editing.

9
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:34.380
Image model is the model behind every picture made while you edit this world: characters,

10
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.314
places, items and the cover.

11
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:41.518
Custom agent instructions tell Studio's chat helper how you like to work,

12
00:00:41.518 --> 00:00:45.683
like keep the world grounded and ask before adding big factions.

13
00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.193
Then API keys.

14
00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:53.854
A key's secret is shown once, when you make it or rotate it, so store it somewhere safe.

15
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.369
These are mine, one per world I build this way, and the black bars are mine too.

16
00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:01.080
Never show a key on stream.

17
00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.933
The API docs button opens the docs.

18
00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:10.500
The Creator API lets approved accounts read, edit, validate and publish worlds,

19
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:16.701
and it edits the same draft Studio does, so with Studio open you watch the changes land.

20
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:21.137
It covers worlds, saved revisions you can restore,

21
00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:25.108
publishing, mods, images and your world's numbers.

22
00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:29.644
And it has limits on how many requests you can send each minute,

23
00:01:29.644 --> 00:01:32.765
with tighter ones for edits and the costly calls.

24
00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:38.771
Every part of the Workshop world in this series went in through the API.

25
00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:44.590
Read the world, change it, have Voyage check it, then save it, and Studio shows the result.

26
00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.537
Not every account has the API yet, though: other accounts need Studio access and the rollout.

27
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:54.125
That's settings and the API.

28
00:01:54.125 --> 00:02:00.153
Next time, the last basic episode: checking your own world before players do.

29
00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.548
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

